Corpus / specification data sources
================================================================================

CommonMark specification (https://github.com/commonmark/commonmark-spec)
License: CC-BY-SA 4.0 (spec prose) / MIT (test tooling)
  - Vendored as conformance/spec/commonmark/spec.json for the CommonMark
    acceptance sweep (CONF-04): tag 0.31.2 (commit 9103e341a973013013bb1a80
    e13567007c5cef6f), generated via the official `test/spec_tests.py
    --dump-tests` script. Measured: 652 examples.

GitHub Flavored Markdown / cmark-gfm (https://github.com/github/cmark-gfm)
License: BSD-2-Clause + MIT (per upstream)
  - Vendored as conformance/spec/gfm/{spec.json,extensions.json} for the GFM
    acceptance sweep (CONF-04): live master branch @ 499789b493 (2026-07-13),
    generated via the same official `test/spec_tests.py --dump-tests` script
    (forked from commonmark-spec's own tooling). Measured: 670 examples in
    test/spec.txt (CommonMark-synced mirror) + 30 examples in
    test/extensions.txt (GFM-only additions: tables, strikethrough,
    autolinks, disallowed-raw-HTML tag filter, footnotes, task lists).
    Deliberately the live split-file source, NOT the frozen 2019
    0.29.0.gfm.13 combined snapshot behind the public gfm.github.io page.
    See conformance/spec/VERSIONS.txt for the full pin record.

Marp-derived golden corpus (https://github.com/marp-team)
License: MIT (@marp-team/marpit, @marp-team/marp-core)
  - conformance/corpus/cases/ holds 18 golden Markdown->HTML(/CSS) cases used as
    conformance ground truth (CONF-01), generated by rendering representative
    Marp Markdown through the REAL @marp-team/marp-core v4.4.0 (which bundles
    @marp-team/marpit) — the npm oracle — via tools/corpus-gen/gen.mjs.
  - Each case declares requires_engine="marp-core"; regenerate with
    `cd tools/corpus-gen && npm ci && node gen.mjs` whenever the marp-core pin or
    the case set changes (re-vendored data asset -> update this block in the same PR).

